    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (2 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` are support classes, not test classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation following the codebase's existing conventions for derived, read-only owner fields (like `displayName`, `membershipTier`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it in the API response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/LocalityResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 A small utility mirroring the style of `AddressNormalizer`: holds the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and resolves any other/`null` city to `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired a new `@Named(\"formatLocality\")` derivation into `toOwnerDto` via `qualifiedByName`, delegating to `LocalityResolver.resolve(owner.getCity())`, consistent with how the other derived fields are mapped.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` expecting `NSW` for Sydney, and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` expecting `UNKNOWN` for an unlisted city) both pass.",
