    "final_verdict": "The change is clean and idiomatic. The mapper already has `format*`/`normalize*` default methods that delegate to util classes (`AddressNormalizer`, `TelephoneNormalizer`), and `LocalityResolver` sits right alongside them following the same final-class/private-constructor/static-method pattern. The `@Named` wiring and Javadoc match the existing members exactly.\n\nVERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe structure is coherent, additive, and matches the established conventions in this codebase:\n\n- **Logic placement is right.** The city\u2192region table and lookup live in a dedicated `LocalityResolver` util class rather than being inlined in the mapper. This mirrors the existing `AddressNormalizer`/`TelephoneNormalizer` utilities that `OwnerMapper` already delegates to, and keeps the fixed table out of the MapStruct interface.\n- **The mapper method fits the established pattern.** `formatLocality` is a `@Named` `default` method with the same null-guard + delegation shape as `normalizeAddress`/`normalizeTelephone`, and the `@Mapping(..., qualifiedByName = \"formatLocality\")` line sits naturally among the sibling derived fields. The Javadoc matches the surrounding members' style (including the standard `@Named` note).\n- **No duplication and no catch-all.** `LocalityResolver` has a single responsibility; `OwnerMapper` is not accreting unrelated logic.\n- **The OpenAPI addition is consistent** \u2014 the `locality` field is placed with the other read-only derived fields and documents the same table.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find this a natural extension of the existing derived-field machinery.",
